+\centering\small
+\setlength{\tabcolsep}{5pt}
+\input{generated/c7_family_influence_summary.tex}
+\caption{C7 family-deletion sensitivity of the further-law lower endpoint $\ell^-$, at $r=16$, in all 24 model/readout conditions. Minima and maxima cover all 64 complete-family deletions, each with its own empirical whitening; they are not confidence intervals. The final column counts endpoints satisfying $\ell^->10^{-8}+10^{-7}|\ell^-|$, out of 64. Zero is an inconclusive bound on strict positivity. Values are rounded only for display; full-precision endpoints and family identities are retained.}
+\label{tab:c7-family-influence}
+\end{table}
+
+\Cref{tab:c7-family-influence} reports every condition. The same 23 conditions exceed the original tolerance after every deletion; Llama-3.2-3B/layer 11 retains a zero lower endpoint throughout. Across the 64 common-family deletions, the equal-cell mean $\ell^-$ ranges from $0.00102081$ to $0.00112915$, compared with $0.00109725$ on the complete bank; the mean upper endpoint ranges from $0.02970592$ to $0.03043969$. Llama-3.1-8B/layer 13 remains the largest contributor, with $\ell^-\in[0.02434807,0.02695796]$ versus $0.02618766$ originally. Deleting family 016 gives its largest reduction, about $7.02\%$; deleting family 044 gives its largest increase, about $2.94\%$. Its share of the lower-endpoint sum remains $99.3822\%$--$99.4776\%$. No single-family deletion removes this positive guarantee or the cross-condition concentration; neither statement measures the unknown true costs.
+
+This sensitivity check supports stability to the declared single-family deletions, while leaving multiple-family effects and shared language-construction biases unresolved. It is not independent-context replication, population inference or evidence about native computation. It does not evaluate alternative registrations: the optional all-image registration LOFO described in \cref{app:bounded-margin-details} remains prepared and unexecuted. The source supplement under \texttt{supplementary/c7\_family\_influence\_v1} retains the complete scalar outputs, input mapping and table formatter; the public project also retains all per-deletion diagnostics and the unchanged executed code. This manuscript revision integrates those completed records without rerunning numerical tests or analysis.
